      "left": {
        "pageNumber": 17,
        "runningHead": "CH. 9 • PROCESS HOLLOWING & ATOMBOMBING",
        "content": "<div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>64-bit KPP (PatchGuard), VBS & Anti-Forensics:</strong> In <strong>64-bit</strong> Windows, Kernel Patch Protection (<strong>KPP</strong> / PatchGuard) prevents rootkits from modifying the <strong>SSDT</strong>, <strong>IDT</strong>, and kernel code pages. <strong>Virtualization-Based Security (VBS)</strong> and Credential Guard isolate credentials in hypervisor containers. Windows Security Event ID <strong>1102</strong> indicates the audit log was deliberately cleared. In Linux memory forensics, <code>struct task_struct</code> represents a running task/process, analogous to Windows <strong>_EPROCESS</strong>.\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"legal-dispatch-header\">\n      <span class=\"badge-primary\">Chapter 9 • Advanced Process Injection</span>\n      <h2>Process Hollowing, AtomBombing & Early Bird APC</h2>\n    </div>\n    <p>Adversaries employ advanced in-memory injection techniques to run malicious payloads completely filelessly:</p>\n\n    <h3>Process Hollowing (RunPE)</h3>\n    <p>Process Hollowing follows a precise 5-step operational lifecycle:</p>\n    <ol>\n      <li>Spawn a legitimate binary (e.g., <code>svchost.exe</code>) in a <strong>SUSPENDED</strong> state using <code>CreateProcess(CREATE_SUSPENDED)</code>;</li>\n      <li>Unmap/hollow out the original code section from the process address space using <code>NtUnmapViewOfSection</code>;</li>\n      <li>Allocate new memory at the original base address using <code>VirtualAllocEx</code> with RWX permissions;</li>\n      <li>Write the malicious payload into the unmapped hollow using <code>WriteProcessMemory</code>;</li>\n      <li>Adjust thread execution context (updating <code>EIP</code>/<code>RIP</code>) using <code>SetThreadContext</code> and resume execution with <code>ResumeThread</code>.</li>\n    </ol>\n\n    <h3>AtomBombing & Early Bird APC Injection</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>AtomBombing:</strong> Abuses Windows <strong>Global Atom Tables</strong>. The injector stores shellcode inside an atom table and forces the target process to retrieve the shellcode into its address space via Asynchronous Procedure Calls (<strong>APCs</strong>), bypassing traditional <code>WriteProcessMemory</code> API hooks!</li>\n      <li><strong>Early Bird APC Injection:</strong> Queues a malicious APC to the main thread of a suspended process using <code>QueueUserAPC</code> before the application's entry point executes. When the thread resumes, the APC fires <em>before</em> security software hooks and EDR sensors initialize!</li>\n    </ul>"
      },
      "right": {
        "pageNumber": 18,
        "runningHead": "DLL HOLLOWING & DOPPELGÄNGING",
        "content": "<div class=\"legal-dispatch-header\">\n      <span class=\"badge-primary\">Stealth Execution Techniques</span>\n      <h2>DLL Hollowing, Doppelgänging & Herpaderping</h2>\n    </div>\n    <h3>Module Overwriting & Transaction Attacks</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>DLL Hollowing (Module Overwriting):</strong> Loads a legitimate, rarely-used DLL signed by Microsoft into memory and overwrites its <code>.text</code> code section with malicious shellcode. Because the memory is backed by a legitimate file on disk, basic unbacked memory scanners (like <code>malfind</code>) are bypassed!</li>\n      <li><strong>Process Doppelgänging:</strong> Abuses NTFS Transactions (<strong>TxF</strong>). An attacker creates a transacted file, writes payload bytes to it, creates a section object from the transaction, rolls back the transaction (so nothing touches disk!), and launches the process from the memory section.</li>\n      <li><strong>Process Herpaderping:</strong> Modifies the source executable file on disk after the memory section is mapped but before thread execution begins, confusing security tools that inspect disk files matching running PIDs.</li>\n      <li><strong>Reflective DLL Injection:</strong> Injects a DLL directly into memory without calling <code>LoadLibrary</code> by embedding a custom <code>ReflectiveLoader</code> function that resolves imports and relocations in-memory.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Exam Rule on Code Injection:</strong> Process Hollowing unmaps code using <code>NtUnmapViewOfSection</code>. AtomBombing uses <strong>Global Atom Tables</strong>. Early Bird queues an APC via <code>QueueUserAPC</code> to fire before EDR hooks load. DLL Hollowing overwrites legitimate signed module <code>.text</code> sections.\n    </div>\n\n    \n        <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-banner\">\n          <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-info\">\n            <span style=\"font-size: 1.1rem; margin-right: 8px;\">🎯</span>\n            <div>\n              <strong style=\"font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--text-heading);\">Test Your Mastery: Spread 9</strong>\n              <div style=\"font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-muted);\">Practice all 10 targeted exam questions (Q81–Q90) on Advanced In-Memory Code Injection.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <button class=\"btn-tool btn-mcq\" onclick=\"window.openMCQForSpread(8)\" style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 6px 14px;\">Start Quiz (Q81–Q90) →</button>\n        </div>"
      }
